Playwright Library (playwright)
This is the core Node.js library that gives you low‑level control over browsers — Chromium, Firefox, WebKit. 
The things you can do:
Launching browsers, Creating browser contexts and pages, Navigating, clicking, filling forms, Taking screenshots etc..
the things you cannot do:
Test frameworks, assertions, or reporting by itself.

Playwright Test (‘@playwright/test’)
This is Playwright Library + a test runner.
The things you can do:
A full test framework, Built-in assertions, Auto-waiting, retries, timeout settings, Parallel test execution, Built-in reporting, tracing, screenshots, videos and fixtures for the intialzation.
